{"cluster_id": "C-0364", "topic": "CAS blob protocol", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B050-003", "B050-014"], "canonical_claim": "The generation-8 canonical snapshot wire remains byte-identical, retains mandatory `\"lc\":\"live\"`, and does not bump `G_BUILD`. Additionally, The generation-8 snapshot byte golden still begins with `{\"type\":\"cas_ref_snap\",\"v\":8}` and retains the same ordered `\"lc\":\"live\"` metadata field.", "issue_ids": ["T5"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/task-5-step9-c-brief.md#L9-L9", ".superpowers/sdd/task-5-step9-c-report.md#L21-L23"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0365", "topic": "CAS blob protocol", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B050-004", "B050-015"], "canonical_claim": "Snapshot encoding writes literal `lc = live`; decoding requires the `lc` field and accepts exactly `live`. Additionally, `writeSnapshotMeta` writes `live`, `decodeRefTableSnapshot` requires `lc`, and decoding rejects every `lc` value other than `live`.", "issue_ids": ["T5"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/task-5-step9-c-brief.md#L10-L10", ".superpowers/sdd/task-5-step9-c-report.md#L24-L25"]}
