{"cluster_id": "C-0369", "topic": "CAS blob protocol", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B051-063"], "canonical_claim": "The object-storage interface provides `removeObjectIfTokenMatches` for token-exact deletion and `copyObjectConditional` for write-once server-side copy with `If-None-Match: *`, both with fail-closed defaults.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/upstream-patch-inventory.md#iobject-storage-h"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0370", "topic": "CAS blob protocol", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M-014"], "canonical_claim": "The build writes a precommit binding to a /_precommits namespace shard before publish, giving GC visibility into in-flight blobs; the fold barrier holds the +1 edge until the manifest body is present. Publish is one CAS PUT to the ref shard updating refs[part_name] and appending {+, name, T} to the journal atomically; tokened deps are edge-protected (EDGE-BEFORE-OBSERVE) and not re-checked at promote, while non-tokened deps get a per-hash .meta point-read and copy-forward-if-condemned inline in the blob-revalidation loop.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/01-architecture.md#write-path-overview"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0371", "topic": "CAS blob protocol", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-012"], "canonical_claim": "CAS's condemned detection is a per-hash `.meta` point-read (`BlobMeta{version, state, condemn_round, size}` with `MetaState::Clean`/`Condemned`), not a writer-side retired-view cache; the earlier `Store::syncRetiredView`/`observed_gc_round`/`view_gate` machinery and the `MountLease.observed_gc_round` field are removed entirely. GC always writes a `Condemned` meta before ever deleting the body, so an absent meta reads exactly as live as a `Clean` one.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/03-writer-protocol.md#L102-L129"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0372", "topic": "CAS blob protocol", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-013"], "canonical_claim": "The writer consults the per-hash `.meta` with a single GET (`loadMeta`) only at `Build::observeAndAdmit` (dedup-hit/adopt path) and `Build::uploadFromSource` (fresh-upload/condemned-displacement path); a `Clean` or absent meta is adopted for free, a `Condemned` meta throws `ABORTED` so the caller re-uploads from source (INV-1) rather than reading the dying object.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/03-writer-protocol.md#L121-L129"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0373", "topic": "CAS blob protocol", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-014"], "canonical_claim": "EDGE-BEFORE-OBSERVE manifest-trust adoption: for a tokenless W-EVIDENCE dependency naming a blob referenced by a live committed source manifest, `Build::promote` trusts the durable manifest edge (`isTrustedAdopt`) with NO per-file HEAD/GET, because the source pins the blob (in-degree >= 1, GC cannot condemn it) and this build's own precommit edge is re-proved live at the promote owner-liveness gate before the trust fires; `copyForwardFromCondemned`/`isCopyForwardableTokenless` are deleted as a result.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/03-writer-protocol.md#L242-L263"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0374", "topic": "CAS blob protocol", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-121"], "canonical_claim": "The pluggable blob-hash Phase 1 design encodes the hash algorithm identifier directly in the blob's storage path (`blobs/<algo>/<shard>/<hex>`), records the pool's chosen algorithm in `PoolMeta`, and fail-close-validates that recorded algorithm against the disk's configured algorithm on every open, so an existing pool is never silently re-hashed under a different algorithm.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-11-unattended-cas-campaign.md#L147-L152"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0375", "topic": "CAS blob protocol", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-187"], "canonical_claim": "The content-hash algorithm (CityHash128) is an unversioned, unpinned pool contract (AD1-3): a future change to the hash algorithm would silently fork dedup and break relink, because nothing pins or versions which hash algorithm a pool's content-addressed keys were computed with.", "issue_ids": ["AD1-3"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L1184-L1185"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0376", "topic": "CAS blob protocol", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-292"], "canonical_claim": "`CasEnvelope` is a 70-byte little-endian core header (magic, writer_version, compatibility_version, hash_algo, flags, header_len, domain_id[16], incarnation_tag[16], build_id[16], header_hash[8]) followed by TLV extensions padded to a per-pool fixed `header_len`, so blob payloads always start at a constant offset for a constant-shift `locate`; `logical_size`/`logical_hash` core fields were dropped 2026-07-11 to let the header be built before the payload streams (S3-native staging).", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/02-store-core.md#3-4-on-storage-formats-with-versioning-confirmed"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0377", "topic": "CAS blob protocol", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-293"], "canonical_claim": "`CasBlobMeta` (the `.meta` freshness sibling) is a fixed `CAMT`-magic codec with `BODY_LEN=22` (magic[4]+version[1]+state[1]+condemn_round[8 LE]+size[8 LE]); `version` must equal 1 and `state` must be Clean=0 or Condemned=1, else decode fail-closes.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/02-store-core.md#3-4-on-storage-formats-with-versioning-confirmed"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0378", "topic": "CAS blob protocol", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-310"], "canonical_claim": "Plain dedup adoption itself is free of `.meta` write cost (`CasBuild.cpp:337`); an earlier revision of the soak audit mislabeled the dedup-adoption class as carrying `.meta` write tags.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-13-cas-soak-metrics-audit.md#files-written-vs-s3-ops-per-part-workload-table"]}
